# Cross-Platform (Android / Desktop / iOS)

Ships on **desktop, Android, and iOS (RoboVM/MobiVM)**. Shared code must use the **intersection** of those runtimes unless the user scopes a change to one launcher.

Compile target is **Java 11**, but **iOS `robovm-rt` lacks many newer JDK APIs**. Desktop tests can pass while iOS dies with `NoSuchMethodError`. Base-game `master` already avoids streams, `Optional`, `List.of` / `Map.of` / `Set.of`, and `java.util.function` in `core` / `SPD-classes` — keep that on `main`.

## Forbidden on guarded production paths

Guarded by `RoboVMUnsupportedApisTest` (`core`, `SPD-classes`, `desktop`, `android`, `ios` main sources). **Do not** grow a parallel JDK polyfill — rewrite to classic forms; shared helpers only for hot duplicates.

| Avoid                                       | Use instead                                             |
| ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| `String.isBlank()`                          | `Strings.isBlank(s)` (multi-site) or `trim().isEmpty()` |
| `String.join(...)`                          | `Strings.join(...)` or local `StringBuilder`            |
| `java.util.Base64`                          | `Base64Codec` (same RFC 4648 strings)                   |
| `java.util.function.*`                      | Nested interface next to owner, or `Callback`           |
| `java.util.Optional`                        | Nullable return / empty collections                     |
| `List.of` / `Map.of` / `Set.of`             | `Collections.empty*()` or `new ArrayList<>()` etc.      |
| `list.sort(...)`                            | `Collections.sort(list, comparator)`                    |
| `Comparator.comparing*`                     | Anonymous `Comparator` / `Integer.compare`              |
| `Map.getOrDefault` / `Map.merge`            | `containsKey` / `get` + `put`                           |
| `Collection.removeIf`                       | Iterator remove loop                                    |
| `java.nio.file` for game data               | `FileUtils` / `java.io` streams                         |
| Desktop cwd / `System.getenv` in `<clinit>` | Build-time defaults + `FileUtils` Local                 |

Lambdas / method references already exist in this fork and are OK when they do not pull in forbidden APIs. Prefer **anonymous `Comparator`** (master style) for new sorts.

Extend `RoboVMUnsupportedApisTest` when adding a new forbidden pattern.

## org.json (master warning — crashes on Android/iOS)

`Bundle` documents this: the Android runtime’s `org.json` is incomplete; MobiVM uses it on iOS too. Desktop-only methods **crash on device**.

- Stick to APIs in [Android org.json](https://developer.android.com/reference/org/json/package-summary)
- Prefer going through `Bundle` for game state
- Do not use desktop-only helpers (e.g. `JSONObject.keySet()`, `write`, non-String `JSONTokener` constructors) — see comments in `Bundle`

## Structure & persistence

- Gameplay in `core` / `SPD-classes`; launchers stay thin. Native APIs only under `desktop/` `android/` `ios/` when needed.
- Persist via `FileUtils` Local sandbox (`FileUtils.setDefaultFileProperties(Files.FileType.Local, "")` in launchers) — not `new FileOutputStream("…")` relative to cwd.
- UI: touch + keyboard/mouse; safe insets via `Game.platform` / `PlatformSupport`.

## Before finishing

- [ ] Logic in `core` / `SPD-classes` (or intentional per-launcher work)
- [ ] No forbidden JDK APIs; org.json usage Android-safe
- [ ] No desktop-only assumptions on shared paths
- [ ] Mobile lifecycle / slow I/O considered for network or disk work
